    {
      "id": "claim_95a1672f2049439dbcf34c6748a0994b",
      "statement": "Codependix deliberately duplicates ESLint's depConstraints as boundary rules because codependix reads the Nx project graph (seeing implicit edges) while ESLint reads import statements (seeing only explicit edges), so codependix gates at least as much and sometimes more.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://configuration/ic-suite/codependix.config.ts#L100-L150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fecd26250ed0b82b6e51fbe38192832e41d9b9be14f1e0c55bf8660b9449b0e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d753cb086e674971933640220bee0c80",
      "statement": "Core vocabulary: Graph (one level built by one package), Neighborhood (a project's one-hop dependencies and dependents), Workspace Graph (the whole-repo graph exported once), Export (descriptive JSON or Markdown), Boundary (prescriptive allow, forbid or acyclic rules producing violations), and Anchor (codependix-owned comment markers independent of conformetry).",
